language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Magic square of size n: fill an n x n grid with the integers 1 to n*n, each used once, so that every row, column and both diagonals sum to n(n^2+1)/2.
given n : int(1..)
find square : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int(1..n*n)

branching on [square]
heuristic sdf
such that
$ each cell contains a different integer
allDiff([square[i,j] | i : int(1..n), j : int(1..n)]),
$ each row sums to the magic constant n(n^2+1)/2
forAll i : int(1..n) . ((sum j : int(1..n) . square[i,j]) = (n*(n*n+1))/2),
$ each column sums to the magic constant n(n^2+1)/2
forAll j : int(1..n) . ((sum i : int(1..n) . square[i,j]) = (n*(n*n+1))/2),
$ the main diagonal sums to the magic constant n(n^2+1)/2
((sum i : int(1..n) . square[i,i]) = (n*(n*n+1))/2),
$ the anti-diagonal sums to the magic constant n(n^2+1)/2
((sum i : int(1..n) . square[i,n+1-i]) = (n*(n*n+1))/2)
